      "response": {
        "id": "msg_011CdzXQU2Ugh4soKqN1dUZc",
        "container": null,
        "content": [
          {
            "citations": null,
            "text": "# Two Key Aspects of Photosynthesis\n\n1. **Light-dependent reactions (Light Reactions)**\n   - Occur in the thylakoid membranes of chloroplasts\n   - Capture light energy and convert it into chemical energy (ATP and NADPH)\n   - Produce oxygen as a byproduct from splitting water molecules\n\n2. **Light-independent reactions (Calvin Cycle)**\n   - Occur in the stroma of chloroplasts\n   - Use ATP and NADPH from light reactions to convert carbon dioxide into glucose\n   - Also called carbon fixation or the \"dark reactions\" (though they don't require darkness)",
            "type": "text"
          }
        ],
        "model": "claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929",
