            "role": "user",
            "content": "Given these aspects:\n# Two Key Aspects of Photosynthesis\n\n1. **Light-dependent reactions (Light Reactions)**\n   - Occur in the thylakoid membranes of chloroplasts\n   - Capture light energy and convert it into chemical energy (ATP and NADPH)\n   - Produce oxygen as a byproduct from splitting water molecules\n\n2. **Light-independent reactions (Calvin Cycle)**\n   - Occur in the stroma of chloroplasts\n   - Use ATP and NADPH from light reactions to convert carbon dioxide into glucose\n   - Also called carbon fixation or the \"dark reactions\" (though they don't require darkness)\nWrite one sentence connecting them."
          }
        ]
      },
